# OSV acquisition policy successor — 2026-11-16

Authorized scope: implement one OSV temporal rule measured from the last successful
download, audit conflicting active policy/tests/docs, preserve Trivy/Grype and
advisory exceptions. No commits/publication, real downloads or complete run.
Central files are read-only under current permissions: prepare a reviewed patch
locally and apply only through the host escalation mechanism.

Full SDD route / high complexity: persisted acquisition state, scanner gates,
concurrent preparation and recovery change. Parent feature: scripts-toolbox-native,
with documentary succession in scripts-toolchain-config. Existing broad ACs remain
UNVERIFIED; the bounded manual criteria below do not replace Docker qualification.

## Criteria

OSV-01: Ox accepts a structurally valid OSV report when upstream data is older than
24h; no local upstream age threshold remains. Trivy/Grype age rules and advisory
exceptions remain intact. Missing/mismatched provenance still fails integrity.
OSV-02: base absent, acquisition unknown or acquisition strictly older than 12h
causes acquisition; <=12h reuses; repeated analyses do not change acquisition time.
OSV-03: every successful OSV download, including manual and identical-content
updates, saves acquisition time; failed download/validation does not renew it.
OSV-04: validated immutable snapshots replace the active pointer atomically;
old bytes used by an in-flight scan survive; concurrent starts serialize acquisition.
OSV-05: current guides/configs/tests/ADRs consistently express the single rule;
historical evidence remains identifiable and unmodified. Independent review and
validation assess current observed inputs, not implementation declarations.

## Decision, risk and ownership

D-31: central Toolbox owns the 12h acquisition clock and acquisition receipt. Ox
retains provenance integrity and findings checks, removing its competing 24h
upstream veto. Timestamps from upstream are provenance, not OSV expiry signals.
Do not replace the 24h limit with a second local 12h limit or reset time on reads.
Migrate a valid legacy receipt bound to the same snapshot with its exact timestamp;
unknown/mismatched receipt requires acquisition rather than inference from mtime.
Existing current.json acquisition always takes precedence over legacy receipt.
Download and validate before publishing; retain immutable historical snapshots.
R-31: receipt/pointer inconsistency or manual update without receipt could renew
incorrect data or trigger repeated acquisition; test publication and failure paths.

Coordinator owns scripts/lib/backends.sh, scripts/config/automation.json,
scripts/tests/test_database_age.py, scripts/tests/test_backends.py,
tools/governance/tests/test_security_quality.py and common Ox documentation.
central_patch owns only a disposable central copy, central tests and external
patch/applicator. Review/validation use fresh independent contexts, read-only
implementation. No specialist subdelegation; tree budget is root + coordinator +
two specialists. Profile/context creation observed available; completion/vacancy
will be established by actual subsequent creation. Extra-high effort not needed.

Primary skill selected, read and applied: software-delivery,
.codex/skills/software-delivery/SKILL.md (unversioned); bridge
sdd/chain/software-delivery.md version 1. Reference consulted:
references/build-inputs-and-trust.md. Contribution: separate acquisition/cache
identity from scan policy, preserve verified immutable inputs and qualify failure
and recovery with offline fixtures. No external lookup needed for local contracts.

## Sequence and verification

1. T031: record authorization/criteria and inspect actual callers and state.
2. T032: implement Ox policy and stage central acquisition/receipt correction.
3. T033: independent review of both implementations and audit docs/tests.
4. T034: apply reviewed central patch through authorized escalation; execute focused
   offline tests and input manifests. Do not run scanners/download real data.
5. T035: independent validation against OSV-01..05, document exact limitations and
   run parent feature checker without promoting its broader unverified ACs.

